{"segs": ["PA_ja_246:0.2", "PA_ja_246:0.3"], "en": "The Second Book of Pairs, The Chapter on the Jackal (Siṅgālavagga)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_246:0.4"], "en": "6. The Bālavādajātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_246:1.1", "PA_ja_246:1.2"], "en": "\"Having killed, having cut, and having struck, the unrestrained man gives a gift.\"", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_246:1.3"], "en": "Eating food that has been prepared for oneself,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_246:1.4"], "en": "one is defiled by evil.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_246:2.1"], "en": "Even if one were to kill one's own children and wife...", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_246:2.2"], "en": "The unrestrained man gives gifts;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_246:2.3", "PA_ja_246:2.4"], "en": "yet even while enjoying them, the wise man is not defiled by evil.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_246:3.1"], "en": "The Sixth Jātaka: The Story of the Advice to a Fool.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
